INT. FUNERAL HOME - CASKET SHOWROOM - DAY

Mahogany, pine, brushed steel. Satin linings in six shades of cream. A single armchair for the grieving. A small fountain gurgles in the corner.

AUGUSTUS PEMBROKE (50s, widower in training, black suit too tight at the shoulder) walks the room with his hat in both hands. He stops at the cheapest casket and touches it with one finger, as though it might be hot.

A SALESMAN (40s, shiny shoes, a lapel pin shaped like a dove) appears out of nowhere at his elbow.

SALESMAN
Good morning, sir. Have you lost someone?

AUGUSTUS
Not yet.

SALESMAN
Ah. A planner. I admire a planner.

AUGUSTUS
My wife's still alive. She's in the car.

SALESMAN
In the car.

AUGUSTUS
She's got a cold. She wanted to wait.

SALESMAN
Of course. We offer a drive-through option, sir, for the living.

AUGUSTUS
Really?

SALESMAN
No.

Augustus nods slowly. The Salesman leans on the pine casket and pats it, as a man pats a horse.

SALESMAN (CONT'D)
This is our Starter. Pine, plain handles, a one-year warranty.

AUGUSTUS
On a casket?

SALESMAN
If it fails, we replace it. Free of charge.

AUGUSTUS
How would you know it failed?

SALESMAN
Sir, that is exactly the question my own father asked.

AUGUSTUS
What did you tell him?

SALESMAN
That we have a very friendly staff. My name is Percival, by the way.

AUGUSTUS
Augustus.

PERCIVAL
Augustus. May I ask what your wife would want?

AUGUSTUS
She'd want me to stop pricing things.

PERCIVAL
She sounds lovely.

AUGUSTUS
She's insufferable. She's alive.

PERCIVAL
Then why are you here?

AUGUSTUS
Because she told me to. She said, Gus, pick something so I don't have to hear about it.

PERCIVAL
Ah. A woman who delegates. I'd like to meet her.

AUGUSTUS
She'd like to meet you too. She's been waiting forty minutes.

PERCIVAL
In the car?

AUGUSTUS
In the car.

Percival straightens. He glances at the door, then back, and for the first time he looks worried.

PERCIVAL
Sir, you left her in a parked vehicle with a cold?

AUGUSTUS
With the heater on.

PERCIVAL
How long?

AUGUSTUS
I told you. Forty minutes.

PERCIVAL
Forty minutes in a car with the engine running?

AUGUSTUS
(beat)
Oh.

They look at each other. Then they both run for the door, Augustus knocking over the fountain, Percival clutching his dove pin, a pair of grown men in dark suits sprinting through a showroom of empty beds.
